NAME
     cksum - CRC-32 and byte count of each file

SYNOPSIS
     cksum [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     cksum prints the CRC-32 and the length of each FILE, or of standard
     input, one line each: "crc length name", as POSIX cksum prints them.
     The tests use it to show that a guest's data survived something the
     host did to the machine underneath it.

SEE ALSO
     memck(1), cat(1)
